     Under 3.0pl10, the tourist class and the Hawaiian shirt are each
controlled by conditional code that's handled at compile time.  The
#version command will show you what options are compiled into your
copy of the game.  If "Hawaiian shirt" isn't one of the listed options,
then you're out of luck unless you rebuild from sources.

     Under 3.1.0, tourists and Hawaiian shirts are controlled by the
same conditional code; you either have both or neither.  #version will
show "tourists", if they're enabled when compiled, but not bother listing
"Hawaiian shirts" since that's now implied by "tourists".

